  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Signed, Sealed, Delivered**: rare: 7 archived performances [3]\n- **For My Friends**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 3 archived performances [3]\n- **My Baby Specializes**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 3 archived performances [3]\n- **You've Lost That Loving Feeling**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n- **Love Having You Around**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [3]\n- **Two to Tango**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [3]\n- **With a Little Help From my Friends**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 3 archived performances [3]\n- **Pungee $**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 5 archived performances [3]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **soulive2012-03-09.mk21.flac24** (recommended): audience recording; 22 songs; 208 min [1]\n- **soulive2012-03-09.mk21.flac16**: audience recording; 22 songs; 208 min [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Night 9 of the Bowlive 3 run; Nigel Hall Band opened, followed by two Soulive sets [1]\n- Bowlive Horns joined: James Casey and Ryan Zoidis on tenor sax, Eric Bloom on trumpet; George Porter Jr. guested on bass and vocals [1]\n- Night 9 of the Bowlive 3 run; Nigel Hall Band opened, followed by two Soulive sets [2]\n- Guests included Nigel Hall on keys/vocals, Adam Deitch on drums, Mark Whitfield and Adam Smirnoff on guitar [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **soulive2012-03-09.mk21.flac24**: taped by Eric McRoberts; transferred by Eric McRoberts; source: Audience/On Stage [1]. Also: This is a 24-bit version of the recording, not meant for MP3 streaming or CD burning; a CD-quality version exists [1]\n- **soulive2012-03-09.mk21.flac16**: taped by Eric McRoberts; transferred by Eric McRoberts; source: Audience/On Stage [2]. Also: This is the 16-bit version; a higher quality 24-bit version of the recording is available on archive.org [2]",
